# ADR rules

- One decision per file, numbered sequentially (`NNNN-title.md`), with: Status
  (proposed/accepted/superseded), Date, Context, Decision, Alternatives, Consequences — plus
  upgrade/pinning/exit strategy when the decision creates an external dependency.
- Do not fake certainty: an ADR stays `proposed` while investigation remains (ADR 0007 is the
  standing example). Acceptance is the creator's call.
- Never edit an accepted ADR's decision; supersede it with a new ADR that links back.
- Check existing ADRs before proposing architecture changes; contradicting an accepted ADR
  requires a superseding ADR, not a workaround.
